Four features, one combined diff (the hunks are disjoint except sfincs_lib.f90's
build_revision, which names all four tags):

  nj-winddir-fix-1  snapwave_boundaries.f90 -- the SnapWave wind-mode boundary direction
                    bug (FINDINGS 43; hpc/patches/snapwave_winddir_v2.3.3.patch).
  nj-igk-fix-1      snapwave_solver.f90 (IG wavenumber from sigm_ig, not sig) and
                    sfincs_wavemaker.f90 x4 (wavemaker_angfac = max(-sin(phi),0), as
                    v2.4.0) -- hpc/patches/snapwave_igk_wavemaker_v2.3.3.patch.
  nj-igseed-1       snapwave_infragravity.f90 -- fixed random_seed(put=...) before the
                    Herbers component draws, re-set on every call (FINDINGS 44 (c);
                    docs/upstream/snapwave_igseed.patch).
  nj-wmseed-1       sfincs_wavemaker.f90 -- NEW, two parts:
                    (1) initialize_wavemakers: a fixed random_seed(put=...) once, right
                        before the IG wavemaker phase draws (the incident-wave draws
                        continue the same stream). Stock code drew those phases from an
                        unseeded RANDOM_NUMBER, so a wavemaker run never repeated itself
                        (same bug class as igseed). Seed 20121030 + 7919*i, distinct from
                        igseed's 20121029 + 7919*i.
                    (2) update_wavemaker_fluxes: the component phase in CLOSED FORM in
                        absolute model time, cos(2 pi f t + phi0 + dphi*t) in real*8,
                        replacing the accumulated real*4 phi = modulo(phi + dphi*dt, 2 pi).
                        The accumulated phase restarts at a resumed run's new tstart, so
                        each component jumped by dphi*(t_resume - tstart) at a resume
                        (dphi = 2 pi 1e-6/f: 0.0126 rad/s at f = 0.0005 Hz) -- the IG
                        signal was discontinuous there and a different realisation after.
                        t is seconds since tref, which nj_sfincs/restart.py keeps. Same
                        component frequencies (f + dphi/2pi) as stock.
